<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Browser "more" popup sheet.

    Card removed, rows sit flat on the sheet surface, semantic groups
    separated by hairline rules. Section labels were once dropped as
    redundant, then reintroduced (two of them: "This page" / "Library")
    with the bookmark-star redesign: promoting Bookmark out of the list
    into the action-row star reorganised the list around it, and the
    two labels re-anchor the reader over the same rules. Only these two
    groups are labelled — the tabs group (top) and the system group
    (Settings/Quit, bottom) stay divider-only, matching the mockup.

    Shape (top→bottom):
      1. Drag handle (shared include).                    [pinned]
      2. Site-identity row: favicon + page title +        [pinned]
         hostname. Same identity vocabulary the
         SecuritySheet uses, scoped to "act on this
         page". Stays pinned — it's the anchor, scrolling
         the title away would lose the context the rest
         of the rows act on. Dismiss is swipe-down or
         scrim-tap; no inline X — the drag handle and the
         taller header read clearly enough as a sheet,
         and dropping the X also drops a second dismiss
         affordance that did the same job.
      3. Identity / quick-row divider.                    [pinned]
      4. ─── scroll boundary ───
      5. Quick-row header: Back · Forward · Bookmark★ · Share · Refresh.
      6. Quick-row / menu divider.
      7. Tabs             — New tab, New private tab
      8. This page        — Find in page, Desktop site, Save snapshot
      9. Library          — Bookmarks, History, Safe Folder
     10. System           — Settings, optional Quit

    The Bookmark★ star is the promoted bookmark toggle; there is no
    longer a "Bookmark page" list row (its add/edit both live on the
    star now).

    Row anatomy:
      • 56dp tall, 16dp horizontal padding — the M3 one-line
        list-item height, shared with the Home popup and the
        OptionsAdapter sheets so every menu row in the app reads
        at the same rhythm; each row is icon + single line
      • TextView with drawableStartCompat icon at 16dp drawablePadding,
        TitleMedium / 16sp text (M3 list-item headline size),
        onSurfaceVariant
      • Desktop site carries a MaterialSwitch as duplicate-parent-state
        status (whole row is the click target)
      • Everything else has no trailing element — the ripple is enough

    State handling stays in the fragment:
      • Bookmark STAR (in the quick-row header, not this list) flips
        its icon/label/tint between outline·"Bookmark" and filled·amber
        ·"Saved" based on mHasBookmark, and toggles the bookmark in
        place (add/delete on the shared repository) with an Edit/Undo
        confirmation toast — see applyStarState / onBookmarkStarClicked.
      • Quick-row labels drop to icon-only past a width/font-scale
        breakpoint (QuickRowLabels.iconOnly); icons never move.
      • Vault row swaps to Downloads in incognito (icon + label +
        dispatched id).
      • Desktop site switch mirrors the current tab's isDesktop().
      • Quit row stays GONE unless SETTINGS_QUIT_PREF is on; the row
        uses colorPrimary text + tint so the destructive treatment
        matches Downloads' / Bookmarks' Delete row.
-->
<!--
    Root mirrors BrowserOptionHolderSheetDialogFragment: a FrameLayout whose
    single child (popup_content) is sized in code to visibleRect.height() -
    mActionBarSize, so the sheet wraps to the SAME height as the Captured sheet
    (sits just under the toolbar). The inner NestedScrollView is weighted, so
    the pinned header stays put and the rows scroll.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/popup_content"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical">

    <include
        layout="@layout/dialog_drag_handle" />


    <!-- Site identity. Mirrors the SecuritySheet's identity block
         (favicon + title + host) so the two sheets read as siblings
         on the browser surface. Renders taller than the menu rows
         (minHeight 72dp via 12dp vertical padding) so it reads as a
         header, not just another list row. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/popup_identity"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:minHeight="72dp"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingHorizontal="16dp"
        android:paddingVertical="12dp">

        <!-- 40dp tinted surface tile with the 24dp favicon centred
             inside (8dp padding → 24dp content). DuckDuckGo-style
             frame so transparent / monochrome / oddly-cropped
             favicons still read as a single identity chip rather
             than floating on the sheet. -->
        <androidx.appcompat.widget.AppCompatImageView
            android:id="@+id/popup_identity_favicon"
            android:layout_width="40dp"
            android:layout_height="40dp"
            android:layout_marginEnd="16dp"
            android:background="@drawable/bg_popup_favicon"
            android:contentDescription="@null"
            android:padding="8dp"
            android:scaleType="centerInside"
            tools:src="@drawable/ic_firedown" />

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/popup_identity_title"
                style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleSmall.Emphasized"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                tools:text="EL PAÍS: el periódico global" />

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/popup_identity_host"
                style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.BodyMedium"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                tools:text="elpais.com" />

        </LinearLayout>

    </LinearLayout>


    <!-- Pinned divider seals the identity row off from the scrolling
         content below; the title stays in view as the rest of the
         sheet scrolls past. Matches the visual break the SecuritySheet
         renders between its identity block and its first section. -->
    <View
        style="@style/Firedown.Divider.InCard"
        android:layout_marginTop="8dp" />


    <!-- wrap_content (not 0dp + weight): the sheet hugs its content so it
         opens exactly as tall as the rows need, instead of the root
         match_parent + weighted scroller forcing it to fill the viewport and
         leaving the inner list scrollable even with space to spare. The
         NestedScrollView still scrolls when content genuinely exceeds the
         bottom_sheet_max_height cap, with the identity header above staying
         pinned (it's outside this scroller). -->
    <androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:overScrollMode="never">

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingBottom="8dp">


            <include
                layout="@layout/fragment_dialog_browser_popup_header"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content" />


            <View
                style="@style/Firedown.Divider.InCard"
                android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                android:layout_marginBottom="8dp" />


            <!-- New tab — always opens a REGULAR tab (dispatches
                 R.id.new_tab, which BrowserFragment forces to
                 non-incognito), so from incognito chrome this is the
                 explicit exit-to-normal-tab action. Mirrors the
                 fixed-meaning rows browsers like Chrome/Firefox show. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_new_tab"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/popup_tabs_new"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_tabs_new_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- New private tab — always opens an INCOGNITO tab
                 (dispatches R.id.new_incognito_tab). Fixed meaning in
                 both modes, matching the New tab row above. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_new_incognito_tab"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/open_new_private_tab_2"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_incognito_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <View
                style="@style/Firedown.Divider.InCard"
                android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                android:layout_marginBottom="8dp" />


            <!-- ── This page ──────────────────────────────────────────
                 Group label anchoring the page-context actions. The
                 bookmark row that used to lead this group was promoted
                 to the action-row star above; the label gives the
                 remaining page actions an eye-anchor now that the list
                 was reorganised around the star. Matches the mockup
                 (only "This page" and "Library" are labelled; the
                 tabs / system groups stay divider-separated). -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/popup_group_this_page"
                style="@style/Firedown.PopupGroupLabel"
                android:text="@string/popup_group_this_page" />


            <!-- Find in page — pure action, no trailing element. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_find"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_find_in_page"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_search_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- Desktop site — MaterialSwitch reflects isDesktop().
                 Whole row is the click target; switch is duplicate-
                 parent-state status, not the hit target. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_desktop"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_desktop_site"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_computer_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                <com.google.android.material.materialswitch.MaterialSwitch
                    android:id="@+id/popup_desktop_switch"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="12dp"
                    android:clickable="false"
                    android:duplicateParentState="true"
                    android:focusable="false" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- Save snapshot — archives the live, post-JS page as one
                 self-contained .html (CSS/images inlined, scripts stripped)
                 through the downloader@ extension's snapshot.js. A page
                 action, grouped with the other "act on this page" rows. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_save_snapshot"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_save_snapshot"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_baseline_archive_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <View
                style="@style/Firedown.Divider.InCard"
                android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                android:layout_marginBottom="8dp" />


            <!-- ── Library ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/popup_group_library"
                style="@style/Firedown.PopupGroupLabel"
                android:text="@string/popup_group_library" />


            <!-- Bookmarks. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_bookmarks"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/library_bookmarks"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_bookmarks_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- History. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_history"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/library_history"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_history_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- Vault (Downloads in incognito; the fragment
                 repaints drawableStart + label + dispatched id). -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_vault"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/popup_vault_text"
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/navigation_vault"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_lock_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <View
                style="@style/Firedown.Divider.InCard"
                android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                android:layout_marginBottom="8dp" />


            <!-- Settings. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_settings"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/browser_menu_settings"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_settings_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

            </LinearLayout>


            <!-- Destructive Quit — GONE unless SETTINGS_QUIT_PREF
                 is on. colorPrimary text + drawable tint is what
                 differentiates it. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/popup_quit"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="56dp"
                android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingHorizontal="16dp"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <TextView
                    style="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.TitleMedium"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:drawablePadding="16dp"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:text="@string/delete_browsing_data_on_quit_action"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorPrimary"
                    android:textSize="16sp"
                    app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_logout_24"
                    app:drawableTint="?attr/colorPrimary" />

            </LinearLayout>

        </LinearLayout>

    </androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView>

    </LinearLayout>

</FrameLayout>
